  {
   "id": "zpogaKUIAwAJ",
   "from": "Vince S. Buffalo",
   "author": "b35e99045f6c74c2",
   "date": "2017-09-29T15:44:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Find index?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">You might do best doing some type of join. See: <a href=\"http://dplyr.tidyverse.org/reference/join.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dplyr.tidyverse.org/reference/join.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466721528000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37BhsGZ2TMGT-Rx-inTxrC\">http://dplyr.tidyverse.org/reference/join.html</a></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">For example:</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">library(tidyverse)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"># create your dataframe (as a tibble)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">df &lt;-  tribble(~name,        ~x,   ~y,</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">                    &quot;lund&quot;,        3 ,  32  ,</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">                    &quot;malmo&quot;,    24,  6   ,</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">                    &quot;germn&quot;,      3,   81  ) </div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">other_df &lt;- tibble(x=3, y=32)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">inner_join(df, other_df)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"># A tibble: 1 x 3</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">   name     x     y</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">  &lt;chr&gt; &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;dbl&gt;</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">1  lund     3    32</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">You could also of course do the simple solution:</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">&gt; df[df$x == 3 &amp; df$y==32, ]</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"># A tibble: 1 x 3</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">   name     x     y</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">  &lt;chr&gt; &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;dbl&gt;</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">1  lund     3    32</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">But joins are more extendable to larger problems, more generalizable to special cases, etc.</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">By the way, in the future – it would be helpful if you can provide the code to produce the dataframe you reference. E.g. with tribble as I did above, or the classic way with data.frame. See: <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5963269/how-to-make-a-great-r-reproducible-example\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5963269/how-to-make-a-great-r-reproducible-example&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466721528000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3og_Wlta1fVG4gms6_9pKO\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5963269/how-to-make-a-great-r-reproducible-example</a></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Vince</div></div></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Sep 29, 2017 at 8:30 AM, bic ton <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bict...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>If I have this simple data:</div><div><div><br></div><div>&gt; data</div><div>           name        x    y </div><div>         lund        3   32  </div><div>         malmo    24  6   </div><div>       germn      3   81    </div><div><br></div></div><div>Now to show the name where x=3 and y=32</div><div>with one condition we can do this:</div><div>with(data, name[x==3])<br></div><div>[1] lund<br></div><div><div>Levels: Ago.......</div></div><div><br></div><div>but with two conditions any idea  show the name where x has to equal 3 and y has to equal 32?</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>Bic</div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466721528000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hRWeW1yUOahqnDGclrugP\">http://d-rug.github.io/</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466721528000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2yfIXqy7es22UgVGKbodLO\">https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466721528000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QdH5HNSXcEmYgh4-pThMA\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div></div>"
